### How to Specify the Document

#### **Option 1: Using a File ID (Uploaded File)**
If you upload a file using the **Files API** (`/v1/files`), you can reference it via `file_id`:

```json
{
  "model": "mistral-ocr-latest",
  "document": {
    "type": "file",
    "file_id": "<UUID_OF_UPLOADED_FILE>"
  }
}
```

#### **Option 2: Using a Document URL**
You can directly specify a URL to a document (e.g., PDF, image) in the request:

```json
{
  "model": "mistral-ocr-latest",
  "document": {
    "type": "document_url",
    "document_url": "https://example.com/document.pdf",
    "document_name": "example.pdf"  // Optional
  }
}
```

#### **Option 3: Using an Image URL**
For images hosted at a URL, use the `image_url` field:

```json
{
  "model": "mistral-ocr-latest",
  "document": {
    "type": "image_url",
    "image_url": "https://example.com/image.jpg"
  }
}
